{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T10:14:25.233Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"786da72d0fe287077b6fb46b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:14:25.231Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Class fixes implemented in one publisher shared by checkpoint and baseline writers. Private 0600 staging remains private until final publication; existing access bits, UID and GID are preserved. The final file-generation/byte/metadata comparison and rename are synchronous inside the held lease/lock after all awaited SDK, staging and lease-fence setup. Cleanup verifies staging inode ownership. Exact file revisions intentionally detect whitespace-only and identical-byte inode replacements; this is an artifact revision comparison, not a semantic input comparison. SDK writeFileAtomic exposes only createParentDirectories, with no expected generation or access-policy parameters, so core leases/fencing are retained and the missing final primitive is package-owned. New focused run passed 18 tests and shared publisher coverage is 100/100/100/100. Function-only reverts each fail behaviorally: old checkpoint writer returns success after final-policy foreign replacement and creates 0666 under umask 000; old baseline publisher returns success after foreign replacement during sync and changes 0400 to 0600. Functions restored after each proof. Added packed npm/Bun SDK race cases and permission checks across global, npx/bunx and local CLI paths."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T10:14:25.233Z"}],"before_hash":"876ec976c41401be98aef18d37365ae0afdea8b069ec1713adf2d34f3bfd2e22","after_hash":"edd97d7bc8ebbb83869c38ebe7135522ea8c5dc3203801d